<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian P-Notes - Tenders total A$131.3 mln.</title>
<headline>Australian P-Notes - Tenders total A$131.3 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Promissory note tenders on the Australian commercial paper market picked up markedly on Tuesday as the market got back into full swing after Monday's bank holiday in the New South Wales state.</p>
<p>Supply largely concentrated on early September maturities and included Lend Lease for A$40 million of September 4 dated paper, which fetched a yield of 4.99 percent.</p>
<p>Further forward Graham &amp; Co came for A$11.3 million for November 5, which also went off at 4.99 percent.</p>
